{"text": "English 33 Cleaning and Maintenance Cleaning Cleaning the outside of the indoor unit 1 Turn off the air conditioner and wait until the fan stops. 2 Disconnect the power supply. 3 Use a soft brush or lukewarm damp cloth to clean the exterior. WARNING Soft brush \u2022 Do not clean the appliance by spraying water directly Lukewarm damp cloth onto it. Water entering the unit may result in electric shock or fire that could cause death, serious injury, or property damage: CAUTION \u2022 Do not use an alkaline detergent to clean the indoor unit display. \u2022 Do not use sulphuric acid, hydrochloric acid, or organic solvents such as paint thinner, kerosene, acetone, benzene, or alcohol to clean the unit surfaces. Cleaning the heat exchanger on the outdoor unit 1 Turn off the air conditioner and wait until the fan stops. 2 Disconnect the power supply. 3 Spray water on the heat exchanger to remove dust and other debris. CAUTION \u2022 Do not use sulphuric acid, hydrochloric acid, or organic solvents such as paint thinner, kerosene, acetone, benzene, or alcohol to clean the unit surfaces. \u2022 If you need to inspect or clean the inside of the heat exchanger on the outdoor unit, contact a local service centre for help.", "source": "D:\\Study\\4_Forth Semester\\AI\\project\\MultiAgent_RAG\\data\\Wall-mount Air-Conditioner WindFree 18,000 BTUHr User Manual.pdf", "page": 32}